      "text": "12,7552.\n</answer>.<|User|>That's correct. Now, let's try another one.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 548 and 229? Please solve it using the distributive property of multiplication over addition.\nPlease reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 548 and 229 using the distributive property of multiplication over addition, we can break down the numbers into more manageable parts. The distributive property states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). We can use this property to split the number 229 into 200 + 20 + 9 and then distribute the multiplication over these parts. Let's break it down step by step.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nFirst, we can express 229 as the sum of 200, 20, and 9:.\n\\[ 229 = 200 + 20 + 9 \\]\n\nNow, we apply the distributive property:\n\\[ 548 \\times 229 = 548 \\times (200 + 20 + 9) \\]\n\\[ = 548 \\times 200 + 548 \\times 20 + 548 \\times 9 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate each term separately:\n1. \\( 548 \\times 200 \\):\n\\[ 548 \\times 200 = 548 \\times (2 \\times 100) = (548 \\times 2) \\times 100 \\]\n\\[ 548 \\times 2 = 1096 \\]\n\\[ 1096 \\times 100 = 109600 \\]\n\n2. \\( 548 \\times 20 \\):\n\\[ 548 \\times 20 = 548 \\times (2 \\times 10) = (548 \\times 2) \\times 10 \\]\n\\[ 548 \\times 2 = 1096 \\]\n\\[ 1096 \\times 10 = 10960 \\]\n\n3. \\( 548 \\times 9 \\):\n\\[ 548 \\times 9 = 548 \\times (10 - 1) = 548 \\times 10 - 548 \\times 1 \\]\n\\[ 548 \\times 10 = 5480 \\]\n\\[ 548 \\times 1 = 548 \\]\n\\[ 5480 - 548 = 4932 \\]\n\nNow, we add all these results together:\n\\[ 109600 + 10960 + 4932 = 127552 \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 548 and 229 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{127552} \\]\n</answer>",
