7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     6.\n     ```.\n   - For the bottom left cell (7 x 9):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     63.\n     ```.\n   - For the bottom middle cell (7 x 9):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     63.\n     ```.\n   - For the bottom right cell (7 x 6):.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     42.\n     ```.\n\n4. **Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary:**.\n   - Starting from the bottom right:.\n     ```.\n     3 | 1 | 7.\n     ---------.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     9 |   |   |.\n     6 |   |   |.\n     ---------.\n     6 | 3 | 2.\n     ```.\n   - The diagonal from the bottom right to the middle right gives 2.\n   - The diagonal from the middle right to the top right gives 2 + 3 = 5.\n   - The diagonal from the top right to the top middle gives 7 + 6 = 13 (write 3 and carry 1).\n   - The diagonal from the top middle to the top left gives 1 + 9 + 1 = 11 (write 1 and carry 1).\n   - The diagonal from the top left to the top row gives 3 + 9 + 1 = 13 (write 3 and carry 1).\n\n5. **Read the final product from the top left to the bottom right:**.\n   - The final product is 315,732.\n\nSo, the product of \\(317 \\times 996\\) is:.\n\\[ 317 \\times 996 = 315,732 \\].\n\nThis completes the grid method for multiplication. <|User|>This is really helpful. Can you also show me how to solve this using the area model for multiplication? <｜Assistant｜> <think>.\nCertainly! The area model for multiplication is a visual and conceptual method that breaks down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts, similar to the distributive property. Let's solve \\(317 \\times 996\\) using the area model step by step.\n\