      "text": "620100 + 13780 + 1378 = 634668.\n```.\nSo, the product of 689 and 922 is 634668.\n</answer>.<|User|>That's correct. Can you also show me how to solve this using the distributive property of multiplication over addition? I find it helpful to understand alternative methods.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nCertainly! Using the distributive property of multiplication over addition can simplify the multiplication process. The distributive property states that a(b + c) = ab + ac. We can apply this property to break down the multiplication of 689 by 922 into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\nFirst, let's express 922 as 900 + 20 + 2. Then, we can use the distributive property to break down the multiplication as follows:\n```\n689 \u00d7 922 = 689 \u00d7 (900 + 20 + 2)\n         = 689 \u00d7 900 + 689 \u00d7 20 + 689 \u00d7 2\n```\nNow, we can calculate each term separately:\n1. \\( 689 \\times 900 \\)\n2. \\( 689 \\times 20 \\)\n3. \\( 689 \\times 2 \\)\n\nLet's calculate each term:\n1. \\( 689 \\times 900 = 689 \\times (9 \\times 100) = (689 \\times 9) \\times 100 \\)\n   - First, calculate \\( 689 \\times 9 \\):\n     ```\n     689\n   \u00d7    9\n   ------\n     6201\n     ```\n   - Then, multiply by 100:\n     ```\n     6201\n   \u00d7   100\n   ------\n     620100\n     ```\n\n2. \\( 689 \\times 20 = 689 \\times (2 \\times 10) = (689 \\times 2) \\times 10 \\)\n   - First, calculate \\( 689 \\times 2 \\):\n     ```\n     689\n   \u00d7    2\n   ------\n     1378\n     ```\n   - Then, multiply by 10:\n     ```\n     1378\n   \u00d7   10\n   ------\n     13780\n     ```\n\n3. \\( 689 \\times 2 = 1378 \\) (as calculated earlier)\n\nNow, we add all the results together:\n```\n620100\n+ 13780\n+   1378\n------\n 634668\n```\nSo, the product of 689 and 922 is 634668, which confirms our previous result.\n</think>.<|Assistant|>",
