      "text": "472,340.\n</answer>.<|User|>That's correct. Now, let's try another one.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 552 and 835? Please solve it using the distributive property of multiplication over addition.\nPlease reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 552 and 835 using the distributive property of multiplication over addition, we can break down the numbers into more manageable parts. The distributive property states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). We can use this property to split the numbers 552 and 835 into parts that are easier to multiply.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nLet's break down the numbers 552 and 835 into parts:\n- 552 can be written as \\(500 + 50 + 2\\).\n- 835 can be written as \\(800 + 30 + 5\\).\n\nNow, we will use the distributive property to multiply each part of 552 by each part of 835 and then sum the results.\n\n1. Multiply 500 by 800:\n   \\[\n   500 \\times 800 = 400,000\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 500 by 30:\n   \\[\n   500 \\times 30 = 15,000\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 500 by 5:\n   \\[\n   500 \\times 5 = 2,500\n   \\]\n\n4. Multiply 50 by 800:\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 800 = 40,000\n   \\]\n\n5. Multiply 50 by 30:\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 30 = 1,500\n   \\]\n\n6. Multiply 50 by 5:\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 5 = 250\n   \\]\n\n7. Multiply 2 by 800:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 800 = 1,600\n   \\]\n\n8. Multiply 2 by 30:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 30 = 60\n   \\]\n\n9. Multiply 2 by 5:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 5 = 10\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum all these products:\n\\[\n400,000 + 15,000 + 2,500 + 40,000 + 1,500 + 250 + 1,600 + 60 + 10 = 472,340\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 552 and 835 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{472,340}\n\\]\n</answer>",
