rite the numbers one above the other for clarity, with 923 on top and 128 below it:.\n```.\n  923\n- 128\n------.\n```.\nWe'll start by subtracting the digits in the units place: 3 - 8. Since 3 is smaller than 8, we need to borrow 1 from the tens place. This changes the 3 to 13 and the 2 in the tens place to 1. Now, we can subtract: 13 - 8 = 5.\n```.\n  923\n- 128\n------.\n    5\n```.\nNext, we subtract the digits in the tens place: 1 - 2. Since 1 is smaller than 2, we need to borrow 1 from the hundreds place. This changes the 1 to 11 and the 9 in the hundreds place to 8. Now, we can subtract: 11 - 2 = 9.\n```.\n  923\n- 128\n------.\n   95\n```.\nFinally, we subtract the digits in the hundreds place: 8 - 1 = 7.\n```.\n  923\n- 128\n------.\n  795\n```.\nTherefore, the difference between 923 and 128 is 795.\n</answer>",
