ting the digits in the units place: 4 - 9. Since 4 is smaller than 9, we need to borrow 1 from the tens place. This changes the 4 to 14 and the 7 in the tens place to 6. Now, we can subtract: 14 - 9 = 5.\n```.\n  6\n  704\n- 939\n------.\n    5\n```.\nNext, we subtract the digits in the tens place: 6 - 3 = 3.\n```.\n  6\n  704\n- 939\n------.\n   35\n```.\nFinally, we subtract the digits in the hundreds place: 7 - 9. Since 7 is smaller than 9, we need to borrow 1 from the thousands place. This changes the 7 in the hundreds place to 6 and the 0 in the tens place to 10. Now, we can subtract: 10 - 9 = 1.\n```.\n  6\n  704\n- 939\n------.\n  235\n```.\nTherefore, the difference between 704 and 939 is 235.\n</answer>",
