 we can use it to solve the problem of finding the product of 580 and 777:\n1. Break down 580 into 500 + 80 and 777 into 700 + 70 + 7.\n2. Apply the distributive property, which states that a(b + c + d) = ab + ac + ad.\n3. Multiply each part of 580 by each part of 777 separately:\n   - 500 * 700 = 350,000.\n   - 500 * 70 = 35,000.\n   - 500 * 7 = 3,500.\n   - 80 * 700 = 56,000.\n   - 80 * 70 = 5,600.\n   - 80 * 7 = 560.\n4. Add all these products together:\n   - 350,000 + 35,000 + 3,500 + 56,000 + 5,600 + 560 = 446,660.\n5. Therefore, the product of 580 and 777 is 446,660.\n</think>.\n<answer>Therefore, the product of 580 and 777 is 446,660, as we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property and then add the products together.</answer>.<|User|>Could you also provide an example of how to use the area model to solve this problem? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly, the area model is a visual method that helps us understand the multiplication process by breaking it down into smaller, more manageable parts. Here's how we can use the area model to solve the problem of finding the product of 580 and 777:\n1. Write 580 and 777 as two numbers, one on top of the other.\n2. Break down 580 into 500 + 80 and 777 into 700 + 70 + 7.\n3. Draw a rectangle and divide it into four smaller rectangles, representing the four parts of the multiplication:\n   - One rectangle for 500 * 700.\n   - One rectangle for 500 * 70.\n   - One rectangle for 500 * 7.\n   - One rectangle for 80 * 700.\n   - One rectangle for 80 * 70.\n   - One rectangle for 80 * 7.\n4. Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n   - 500 * 700 = 350,000.\n   - 500 * 70 = 35,000.\n   - 500 * 7 = 3,500.\n   - 80 * 700 = 56,000.\n   - 80 * 70 = 5,600.\n   - 80 * 7 = 560.\n5. Add the areas of all the smaller rectangles together:\n   - 350,000 + 35,000 + 3,500 + 56,000 + 5,600 + 560 = 446,660.\n6. Therefore, the product of 580 and 777 is 446,660.\n</think>.\n<answe