ndth place (the third digit to the right of the decimal point). In this case, it is 0.\n- Since 0 is less than 5, we do not round up the digit in the hundredth place.\n\nTherefore, 0.24043077746 rounded to the nearest hundredth is 0.24.\n\nSo, the result of 110 divided by 457, rounded to the nearest hundredth, is 0.24.\n</answer>",
