orrect. This is a good way to verify the accuracy of the multiplication result.\n\nThank you for your question, and I hope this helps! If you have any more questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask. <|User|>That's a great verification method. Could you also explain how to use the distributive property to break down the multiplication of 329 and 679?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nCertainly! The distributive property of multiplication allows us to break down the multiplication of 329 by 679 into smaller, more manageable parts. We can use the distributive property to express 679 as a sum of its place values and then distribute the multiplication over these sums.\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Express 679 as a sum of its place values:**\n   \\[\n   679 = 600 + 70 + 9\n   \\]\n\n2. **Distribute the multiplication over these sums:**\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 679 = 329 \\times (600 + 70 + 9)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   329 \\times (600 + 70 + 9) = 329 \\times 600 + 329 \\times 70 + 329 \\times 9\n   \\]\n\nNow, we can calculate each of these products separately:\n\n1. **Calculate \\(329 \\times 600\\):**\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 600 = 329 \\times (6 \\times 100) = (329 \\times 6) \\times 100\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 6 = 1974 \\quad \\text{(since \\(329 \\times 6 = 1974\\))}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1974 \\times 100 = 197400\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(329 \\times 70\\):**\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 70 = 329 \\times (7 \\times 10) = (329 \\times 7) \\times 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 7 = 2203 \\quad \\text{(since \\(329 \\times 7 = 2203\\))}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2203 \\times 10 = 22030\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate \\(329 \\times 9\\):**\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 9 = 2961\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the results:**\n   \\[\n   329 \\times 679 = 197400 + 22030 + 2961\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   197400 + 22030 = 219430\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   219430 + 2961 = 221391\n   \\]\n\nSo, using the distributive property, we get:\n\\[\n329 \\times 679